abstract: "norsk-ki-preg is a Markdown skill for Claude removing AI tells from Bokmål and Nynorsk text. A fixed rule bars it from adding names, numbers, dates or sources not in the text. It builds on liste_v2: 475 Bokmål and 175 Nynorsk words and phrases Claude Opus 5.5 and NorMistral-7B overuse in expository text versus Norwegian Wikipedia. The skill was compared with anti-ai-writing v2.1.0 on untouched sets of 20 AI texts and 20 Wikipedia paragraphs per variety, as preregistered in PREREG v2 (sha256 1e810888865cbdd66761dce6db88178f9374a1c5ee8dda3e1f0f694e4633000c). The measure R is the listed markers' rate in AI text after editing, divided by their rate in human-written text. Under the decision rule, the skill is not better: R_English − R_Norwegian was −0.107 [−0.185; −0.039] for Bokmål and −0.055 [−0.122; 0.010] for Nynorsk. It changed human-written text far less: median normalised edit distance (M3) 0.002 and 0.003, against 0.339 and 0.272. It added content to none of 80 texts. anti-ai-writing added named sources or facts absent from the source to 4 of 80. Their accuracy was not checked. Known limitation: the basic rule left 25 of 40 AI texts untouched. Licences: Apache-2.0 for code and skill, MIT for the anti-ai-writing part, CC BY-SA 3.0 for data and liste_v2."
